\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Two-dimensional cross-section illustrating the coupling topology of gravitational field regions. Each circle represents a field region; where adjacent regions overlap (red shading), the fields couple through shared volume. One interior region (red) and its $k = 4$ nearest neighbors (orange) are highlighted, with the four coupling zones visible as lens-shaped intersections. In three spatial dimensions, the simplex theorem (Section~\ref {subsec:k4}) requires $k = d + 1 = 4$ coupling faces per region; these four coupled faces enclose a tetrahedral volume, the field chamber.}}{9}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
